      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure I\u0027ll try that today.\n\nBy the way, in Patchset 2 I encountered a test error due to short Change-Ids (like `Change-Id: I123`) used in `commit-msg_test.sh` tests. Are those short Change-Ids actually valid? They don\u0027t match against the default pattern which requires 40 alphanums: `pattern\u003d\".*/id/I[0-9a-f]\\{40\\}\"`, but of course they do against the fallback `pattern\u003d\".*\"`.",
      "parentUuid": "9b7d3307_9f939a7c",
