      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T15:35:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"malformed\" in the sense that \"Gerrit \u0026 git do not detect it\".  you can put Change-Id lines throughout the commit message in the middle of text, but Gerrit will ignore them all.\n\n\u003e Gerrit does not reject pushes for such commit messages (that contain a single Change-Id).\n\nas Nasser mentioned, that is a per-project Gerrit setting.  if a project has \"Require Change-Id in commit message\" enabled, and there is no Change-Id footer in the commit message that Gerrit recognizes, then it is rejected.\n\nthe local unittests need to reflect the Gerrit server behavior, not what you want to happen locally.",
      "parentUuid": "48ed49d5_d4dd8c1e",
